#: ../../../Lexicon.md:1
msgid "The LLVM Lexicon"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:4
msgid "This document is a work in progress!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:7
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "定義"

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:9
msgid "A"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:11
msgid "**ADCE** :   Aggressive Dead Code Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:14
msgid "**AST** :   Abstract Syntax Tree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:29
msgid "B"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:33
msgid "**BB Vectorization** :   Basic-Block Vectorization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:36
msgid ""
"**BDCE** :   Bit-tracking dead code elimination. Some bit-wise instructions "
"(shifts,     ands, ors, etc.) \"kill\" some of their input bits -- that is, "
"they make it     such that those bits can be either zero or one without "
"affecting control or     data flow of a program. The BDCE pass removes "
"instructions that only     compute these dead bits."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:43
msgid ""
"**BURS** :   Bottom Up Rewriting System --- A method of instruction "
"selection for code     generation.  An example is the     [BURG](http://www."
"program-transformation.org/Transform/BURG) tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:48
msgid "C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:50
msgid ""
"**CFI** :   This abbreviation has two meanings.     Either:     Call Frame "
"Information. Used in DWARF debug info and in C++ unwind info     to show how "
"the function prologue lays out the stack frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:61
msgid ""
"**CIE** :   Common Information Entry.  A kind of CFI used to reduce the size "
"of FDEs.     The compiler creates a CIE which contains the information "
"common across all     the FDEs.  Each FDE then points to its CIE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:66
msgid ""
"**CSE** :   Common Subexpression Elimination. An optimization that removes "
"common     subexpression computation. For example `(a+b)*(a+b)` has two     "
"subexpressions that are the same: `(a+b)`. This optimization would     "
"perform the addition only once and then perform the multiply (but only "
"if     it's computationally correct/safe)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:73
msgid "D"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:75
msgid "**DAG** :   Directed Acyclic Graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:81
msgid ""
"**Derived Pointer** :   A pointer to the interior of an object, such that a "
"garbage collector is     unable to use the pointer for reachability "
"analysis. While a derived pointer     is live, the corresponding object "
"pointer must be kept in a root, otherwise     the collector might free the "
"referenced object. With copying collectors,     derived pointers pose an "
"additional hazard that they may be invalidated at     any {ref}`safe point "
"<safe point>`. This term is used in opposition to     {ref}`object pointer "
"<object pointer>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:90
msgid "**DSA** :   Data Structure Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:93
msgid "**DSE** :   Dead Store Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:96
msgid "E"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:98
msgid ""
"**ento** :   This namespace houses the     [Clang Static Analyzer](https://"
"clang.llvm.org/docs/ClangStaticAnalyzer.html).     It is an abbreviation of "
"[entomology](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entomology)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:108
msgid "F"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:110
msgid "**FCA** :   First Class Aggregate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:113
msgid ""
"**FDE** :   Frame Description Entry. A kind of CFI used to describe the "
"stack frame of     one function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:117
msgid "G"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:119
msgid ""
"**GC** :   Garbage Collection. The practice of using reachability analysis "
"instead of     explicit memory management to reclaim unused memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:123
msgid ""
"**GEP** :   `GetElementPtr`. An LLVM IR instruction that is used to get the "
"address     of a subelement of an aggregate data structure. It is documented "
"in detail     [here](https://llvm.org/docs/GetElementPtr.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:128
msgid ""
"**GVN** :   Global Value Numbering. GVN is a pass that partitions values "
"computed by a     function into congruence classes. Values ending up in the "
"same congruence     class are guaranteed to be the same for every execution "
"of the program.     In that respect, congruency is a compile-time "
"approximation of equivalence     of values at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:135
msgid "H"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:139
msgid ""
"**Heap** :   In garbage collection, the region of memory which is managed "
"using     reachability analysis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:143
msgid "I"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:145
msgid ""
"**ICE** :   Internal Compiler Error. This abbreviation is used to describe "
"errors     that occur in LLVM or Clang as they are compiling source code. "
"For example,     if a valid C++ source program were to trigger an assert in "
"Clang when     compiled, that could be referred to as an \"ICE\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:151
msgid "**ICF** :   Identical Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:154
msgid "**ICP** :   Indirect Call Promotion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:157
msgid ""
"**IPA** :   Inter-Procedural Analysis. Refers to any variety of code "
"analysis that     occurs between procedures, functions or compilation units "
"(modules)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:161
msgid ""
"**IPO** :   Inter-Procedural Optimization. Refers to any variety of code "
"optimization     that occurs between procedures, functions or compilation "
"units (modules)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:165
msgid "**ISel** :   Instruction Selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:168
msgid "L"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:170
msgid "**LCSSA** :   Loop-Closed Static Single Assignment Form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:173
msgid ""
"**LGTM** :   \"Looks Good To Me\". In a review thread, this indicates that "
"the     reviewer thinks that the patch is okay to commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:177
msgid "**LICM** :   Loop Invariant Code Motion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:180
msgid ""
"**LSDA** :   Language Specific Data Area.  C++ \"zero cost\" unwinding is "
"built on top a     generic unwinding mechanism.  As the unwinder walks each "
"frame, it calls     a \"personality\" function to do language-specific "
"analysis.  Each function's     FDE points to an optional LSDA which is "
"passed to the personality function.     For C++, the LSDA contains info "
"about the type and location of catch     statements in that function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:188
msgid "**Load-VN** :   Load Value Numbering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:191
msgid "**LTO** :   Link-Time Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:194
msgid "M"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:196
msgid "**MC** :   Machine Code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:199
msgid "N"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:203
msgid ""
"**NFC** :   \"No functional change\". Used in a commit message to indicate "
"that a patch     is a pure refactoring/cleanup.     Usually used in the "
"first line, so it is visible without opening the     actual commit email."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:209
msgid "O"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:214
msgid ""
"**Object Pointer** :   A pointer to an object such that the garbage "
"collector is able to trace     references contained within the object. This "
"term is used in opposition to     {ref}`derived pointer <derived pointer>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:219
msgid "P"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:221
msgid "**PGO** :   Profile-Guided Optimization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:224
msgid ""
"**PR** :   Problem report. A bug filed on     [the LLVM Bug Tracking System]"
"(https://bugs.llvm.org/enter_bug.cgi)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:228
msgid "**PRE** :   Partial Redundancy Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:231
msgid "R"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:233
msgid ""
"**RAUW** :   Replace All Uses With. The functions `User::"
"replaceUsesOfWith()`,     `Value::replaceAllUsesWith()`, and     `Constant::"
"replaceUsesOfWithOnConstant()` implement the replacement of one     Value "
"with another by iterating over its def/use chain and fixing up all of     "
"the pointers to point to the new value.  See     also     {ref}`def/use "
"chains <iterate_chains>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:242
msgid ""
"**Reassociation** :   Rearranging associative expressions to promote better "
"redundancy elimination     and other optimizations.  For example, changing "
"`(A+B-A)` into `(B+A-A)`,     permitting it to be optimized into `(B+0)` "
"then `(B)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:247
msgid ""
"**RFC** :   Request for Comment. An email sent to a project mailing list in "
"order to     solicit feedback on a proposed change. See also: the {doc}`RFC "
"process     <RFCProcess>` documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:255
msgid ""
"**Root** :   In garbage collection, a pointer variable lying outside of "
"the     {ref}`heap <heap>` from     which the collector begins its "
"reachability analysis. In the context of code     generation, \"root\" "
"almost always refers to a \"stack root\" --- a local or     temporary "
"variable within an executing function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:262
msgid "**RPO** :   Reverse postorder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:265
msgid "**RTTI** :   Run-time Type Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:268
msgid "S"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:272
msgid ""
"**Safe Point** :   In garbage collection, it is necessary to identify     "
"{ref}`stack roots <stack roots>` so that     reachability analysis may "
"proceed. It may be infeasible to provide this     information for every "
"instruction, so instead the information is     calculated only at designated "
"safe points. With a copying collector,     {ref}`derived pointers <derived "
"pointers>` must not be retained across safe     points and {ref}`object "
"pointers <object pointers>` must be reloaded from     stack roots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:282
msgid "**SDISel** :   Selection DAG Instruction Selection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:285
msgid "**SCC** :   Strongly Connected Component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:288
msgid "**SCCP** :   Sparse Conditional Constant Propagation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:291
msgid ""
"**SLP** :   Superword-Level Parallelism, same as {ref}`Basic-Block "
"Vectorization     <lexicon-bb-vectorization>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:295
msgid "**Splat** :   Splat refers to a vector of identical scalar elements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:303
msgid "**SRoA** :   Scalar Replacement of Aggregates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:306
msgid "**SSA** :   Static Single Assignment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:309
msgid ""
"**Stack Map** :   In garbage collection, metadata emitted by the code "
"generator which     identifies {ref}`roots <roots>` within the stack frame "
"of an executing     function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:314
msgid "T"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:316
msgid "**TBAA** :   Type-Based Alias Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:320
msgid "W"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../Lexicon.md:322
msgid "**WPD** :   Whole Program Devirtualization"
msgstr ""
